# Contributing to {{ vars.project_name }}

Use the Origin89 engineering standards through `just skills-sync` and the local
rules in [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md). Inspect existing contracts and callers before
editing. Keep each issue and PR focused and preserve unrelated changes.

Use enums for closed states, validated identifiers and units, and structured
errors. Parse external data at the boundary. Expected I/O failures must not
panic or silently become successful outcomes. Bound retries, queues,
subprocesses, and waits.

For nontrivial behavior, test distinct success, invalid input, boundaries, and
failure/recovery paths. Check the current stable version and compatibility
before adding a dependency, retain the lockfile, and test the declared MSRV.

Run `just fmt`, then `just check`. Checks include formatting, Clippy, tests,
builds, documentation, MSRV, and workflow syntax. Install tools explicitly;
checks do not install them or perform credentialed operations. `just security`
is a separate networked audit.

Use short conventional commit and PR titles and branches such as
`name/task-name`. Preserve Git authorship and signing settings. Do not add
assistant attribution or co-author footers. Preparing work does not authorize
committing, pushing, merging, publishing, or activating jobs.
